      "side": 1,
      "message": "Shall we just do it before passing control to the kernel instead of waiting for a PCR_Read from it?\nIf the kernel never calls PCR_Read, will the NVRAM be committed during Shutdown, for example? If not, then an attacker can load its own kernel, try picking up the password, and reboot if unsuccessful, w/o sending PCR_Read, and not cause the DA counter to increment. Or, there could be other cases when an important NVRAM commit is lost.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 800,
